  nonce: c21e  # c21e
  message: "DONE, and the open question it carried is answered on measurement rather than by a declared number.\n\nTHE MECHANISM. `finalize._demote_stubs_named_as_consumed`, ADR-0057 §14.1. A resolved edge whose `Edge.derived_from` names an unresolved edge in the graph demotes that edge. No name key, no call line, no candidate set — the relation is STATED by the pass that consumed the stub, not reconstructed downstream from a collision-prone four-part key. It runs BEFORE the same-site rule and stamps the same two `meta` keys, which that rule then skips, so one stub is halved once however many rules reach it (otherwise the declared 0.5 factor would be a lie). It is not gated on two anchored producers: a stated derivation needs no second observer.\n\n`derived_from` mixes Symbol and Edge ids; only a reference naming an unresolved EDGE is read as a supersession.\n\nTHE OPEN QUESTION — \"whether a method-call-recovery stamp should be admitted at all\" — ANSWERED: NO, and not by inventing a precision floor.\n\nThe permission is declared per pass (`RegisteredLinker.supersedes_consumed_stub`, default False) and granted on a committed table, `docs/audits/0020-recovery-linker-supersession-precision.md`. That is ADR-0057 §5's citation discipline applied to a different permission, and the default is False because a pass that has not been measured does not get to rank a producer's positive answer below its own.\n\n  GRANTED  inherited-calls-linker      70 of 70 audited correct; 329 of 329 consistent\n                                       with the declared inheritance graph\n  REFUSED  method-call-recovery-linker 16 of 64 wrong\n\nThe refusal is not a judgement call. I checked whether the one shipped quality signal could condition the grant: `disambiguation_fallback` is set on 5 of the 16 wrong and 13 of the 48 right — a 28% wrong rate among flagged versus 24% among unflagged. Gating on it would discard 28% of the wrong edges and 27% of the right ones, which is refusing at random. There is no signal to condition on, so the grant is refused outright rather than conditioned on a number with no derivation. That pass still STAMPS its consumed edge — the provenance is true and useful — it just does not get to demote on it.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE. `hypergumbo survey . --out survey.json`, this repository, single-backend Python:\n  - demotions: **0 -> 329**, superseder origin `inherited-calls-linker` on all 329, zero from method-call-recovery\n  - neither linker's edge count moved (329 and 64) — the stamps add and remove nothing\n  - `derived_from` edges carrying an EDGE reference: **0 -> 393** (the first in this corpus)\nArtifacts: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/rulik_after/survey.json (before), togad_after/survey.json (after).\n\nWHAT IS NOT ASSERTED. That the 259 unaudited `inherited-calls` edges are correct — they are screened against the inheritance graph, not read; the 30-draw random sample bounds that population's wrong rate at <=10% at 95%. That the grant generalises off this repository — one Python-heavy corpus, and `docs/audits/0020` says so. And the 45 supersessions method-call-recovery would have carried stay unrecorded until that pass has receiver evidence to be right with (WI-fihun)."  # c21e
